      "writtenOn": "2022-09-09T16:09:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like all children of named-temp-sensors now only use \"cros-ec,temp-sensor\".  I think you should move the compatible property up one level, leaving the sensor and other properties as children properties.\n\n```\ntemp-sensors {\n    compatible \u003d \"cros-ec,temp-sensor\";\n    ambient {\n        enum-name \u003d \"TEMP_SENSOR_AMB\";\n        sensor \u003d \u003c\u0026temp_ambient\u003e;\n    };\n    cpu {\n        enum-name \u003d \"TEMP_SENSOR_CPU\";\n        sensor \u003d \u003c\u0026temp_cpu\u003e;\n    }\n};        \n```\n\nThis will allow the temp sensor shim to key off of the compatible name like a typical Zephyr driver instead of using the \"named_temp_sensors\" node name.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 61,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "d2d29aa27461f165423b282acf4fac2fc01b8068",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
